##DESCRIPTION
##  Algebra problem: true or false for inequality
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##KEYWORDS('algebra', 'inequality', 'fraction')

## DBsubject('Algebra')
## DBchapter('Fundamentals')
## DBsection('Real Numbers')
## Date('07/01/2018')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserPopUp.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric');

$md   = 'measurement division';
$pd   = 'partitive division';
$opts = [ $md, $pd ];
$ans1 = DropDown($opts, $md);
$ans2 = DropDown($opts, $md);
$ans3 = DropDown($opts, $pd);
$ans4 = DropDown($opts, $pd);
$ans5 = DropDown($opts, $md);
$ans6 = DropDown($opts, $pd);

$yds        = random(3,  9);
$bushels    = random(2,  5);
$flower_bed = random(24, 64, 4);
$juice      = random(2,  6);
$glasses    = random(4,  10, 2);
$track      = random(4,  10);

$city = list_random(
    { from => 'New York',       to => 'Los Angeles', distance => 2790 },
    { from => 'Boston',         to => 'Los Angeles', distance => 2980 },
    { from => 'Philadelphia',   to => 'Seattle',     distance => 2820 },
    { from => 'Chicago',        to => 'Phoenix',     distance => 1752 },
    { from => 'Miami',          to => 'Minneapolis', distance => 1790 },
    { from => 'Washington, DC', to => 'New Orleans', distance => 1084 },
);
$days = random(3, 8);

BEGIN_PGML

For each of the following word problems, determine if it is a partivitive division
(PD) or measurement division (MD) interpretation.

a) If it takes a half-yard of material to make an apron, how many aprons can be made with [$yds] yards of material?   [___]{$ans1}

b) How many half bushels are there in [`[$bushels] \frac{1}{4} `] bushels?  [___]{$ans2}

c) The perimeter of a square flower bed is [$flower_bed] feet.  Find the length of each side?   [___]{$ans3}

d) Mary poured [$juice] cups of juice equally into [$glasses] glasses.  How much was in each glass?   [___]{$ans4}

e) How many laps around a 1/4 mile track make [$track] miles?   [___]{$ans5}

f) We drove [$city->{distance}] miles from [$city->{from}] to [$city->{to}] in [$days] days.  What was our average distance each day?  [___]{$ans6}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Recall the difference between Partitive and Measurement division. 

- Partitive division means the divisor is interpreted as the number of parts.  
The quotient is size of each part.
- Measurement division means the divisor is interpreted as the size of each part. 
The quotient is the number of parts.

a) [$ans1]
b) [$ans2]
c) [$ans3]
d) [$ans4]
e) [$ans5]
f) [$ans6]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();
